in minnesota family members of dante  wright are angry and questioning the  justice system yesterday former police  officer kim potter was sentenced to two  years in prison for fatally shooting  wright last april after potter used her  gun instead of her taser during a  traffic stop david schuman of our  minneapolis station wcco tv reports  i have to live in this nightmare  watching my son shot and killed over  and over again  through tears katie wright pleaded for  the former police officer kim potter to  get the maximum sentence for killing her  son she never once said his name  and for that i'll never be able to  forgive you  potter who had been on the force for 26  years was convicted of first degree  manslaughter two days before christmas  [Music]  potter says she meant to tase right  during a traffic stop last april  but pulled her gun instead shooting  right once in the chest when her time to  speak came a tearful potter looked  directly at  i understand the mother's love  and i am sorry i broke your heart  officer potter made a mistake  that ended tragically  in the end judge regina chu her voice  cracking said potter would serve 24  months a quarter of what she faced  she never intended to hurt anyone  wright's family disappointed with the  sentence this lady  got a slap on the wrist and we still  every night  sitting around crying  waiting on my sons to come home  under minnesota law potter will only  have to serve two-thirds of her sentence  in prison 16 months meaning she could be  released almost exactly two years after  dante wright's death for cbs saturday  morning david schuman minneapolis
 

